  <p><strong>Course #:</strong> <span data-field="course_number">{{ course_number }}</span>: Community Corrections and Correctional Counseling (3-0) Focuses on an examination of methods used by correctional officers in rehabilitating criminal offenders in community settings.</p>

  <p><strong>Course Description:</strong> This course will examine the history, philosophy and practice of community based correctional programs as alternatives to incarceration, such as pretrial services, probation, and other intermediate sanctions such as boot camps, residential facilities, electronic monitoring, restitution, and community service. We will also examine community corrections as a function of community reentry and parole from prison.</p>

